# The OOF residual dataset is ~70 MB of derived data, more than twenty times
# the largest blob this repository otherwise tracks, so it is excluded here and
# identified by hash instead. Its SHA256 is recorded in
# SHA256SUMS.residuals.txt and residual_manifest.json, together with the
# raw-input fingerprints, seed and code SHA needed to rebuild it byte-for-byte
# with 02_build_oof_residuals.py. Every small artifact -- the factor spec,
# loadings, diagnostics, validation report and manifests -- is committed.
#
# The bytes were committed once, in 43e4d2a, before this exclusion landed, so
# they remain in this branch's history and cannot be removed without a force
# push. Because the file is untracked at the branch head, a squash merge
# carries only the hash into the target branch, not the blob.
oof_gaussian_residuals.parquet
